Creamy Corn Miso Pasta
  --Andee Gosnell

8 oz campanelli pasta (~3 c)
2x10 oz each ears fresh corn, shucked (1 1/2 c corn kernels)
3 tbsp unsalted butter
1 yellow onion, finely chopped (~1 c)
3/4 tsp grated garlic (from 2 small cloves)
1/2 c water
2 tbsp white miso
1/2 tsp gochugaru flakes (Korean chile flakes)
4 tbsp chopped fresh chives, divided
1 oz Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese, grated (~1/4 c) + more for garnish
1 tbsp fresh lemon juice
Kosher salt, to taste

Bring a medium pot of salted water to a boil over high. Cook pasta according to package directions for al dente; drain, reserving 1 c of the cooking water.  Set both aside separately. While water is coming to a boil, place corn on a cutting board and use a sharp chef’s knife to remove kernels from cobs. Place kernels in a medium bowl. Using the back of a knife or a spoon, scrape cobs over bowl to extract any excess corn and corn milk; set aside. Melt butter in a large skillet over medium. Add onions; cook, stirring occasionally, until translucent, ~3 min. Add garlic; cook, stirring constantly, until fragrant, ~1 min. Add corn, along with any corn milk; cook, stirring occasionally, until just beginning to soften and mixture appears dry, ~3 min. Add water; cook, stirring frequently, until most of the water evaporates and corn is tender, 3-4 min. Remove from heat and transfer 1/2 c of the corn mixture to a small bowl; set aside. Transfer remaining corn mixture to work bowl of a food processor; do not wipe skillet clean.  Process corn in food processor until finely chopped and almost smooth, ~20 s. Add 1/4 c of the reserved corn mixture and pulse 2 more times. Set aside. Heat processed corn mixture in reserved skillet over medium until warmed through, ~1 min. Whisk in miso and 1/2 c of the reserved cooking water until combined. Add gochugaru flakes, drained pasta, and 3 tbsp of the chives into corn mixture and gently stir until pasta is coated in a creamy sauce, ~1 min. Remove from heat; stir in Parmigiano-Reggiano and remaining 1/2 c cooking water, 1 tbsp at a time until pasta is coated and creamy. Stir in lemon juice; add salt to taste (if needed) and divide pasta mixture evenly among 4 bowls, and top evenly with remaining 1 tbsp chives, reserved 1/4 c corn mixture, and sprinkle with additional Parmigiano-Reggiano. Serve immediately. 
  

